{"id": "EUVD-2026-102341", "enisaUuid": "23dafd63-cb7d-3bbb-864f-23861e3ce494", "description": "pfSense CE 2.7.0 through 2.9.0 contains a command injection vulnerability in services_captiveportal_hasync.php that allows users with only the Captive Portal HA privilege to execute commands as root. Attackers can set backwardsyncip to a malicious XMLRPC server returning connected_users with shell metacharacters in ip or mac fields, which captiveportal_load_pfctl passes unescaped to a pfctl shell command.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:11:20", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-cp-ha-pfctl", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/captiveportal.inc#L2958-L2966", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/services_captiveportal_hasync.php#L106-L140", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.7.0-through-2.9.0-command-injection-via-captive-portal-ha-sync"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111229", "GHSA-xf3x-9wqm-925c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 6.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "959413c6-a7f7-3865-9800-bfe4854fe630", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.7.0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a63221e0-cf44-3394-b3f4-fa1f40dac50e", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}